# Backend

Stack: Node.js JavaScript, Fastify, PostgreSQL, Drizzle, authenticated WebSocket, JWT with rotating refresh tokens, private AWS S3 attachments.

Inspect the relevant Fastify module first (`backend/src/modules/<name>/`). Reuse existing routes, schemas, and services. Do not introduce parallel APIs.

Respect conversation/group membership checks. Preserve JWT/session security, refresh-token rotation, and replay detection (`refresh_reuse`). Do not weaken cookies/CSRF/native token handling.

Do not add migrations unless the requested behavior needs schema changes. Do not rewrite database or WebSocket architecture.

Use existing attachment multipart APIs. Voice calls are live-only; never store recordings or call history.

Test the affected module first (`backend/src/tests/` or the module's unit tests).
